WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.600
-Our next guest

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.903
is known as the Foodie Magician

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.371
and travels all over the world

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.940
performing magic, mentalism,
and comedy.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.109
Please welcome Josh Beckerman!

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.711
[ Cheering and applause ]
-What's up? Good to see you.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:12.979
-Welcome.
-Honored to be here.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.981
[ Rimshot ]
Thank you for being here.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.482
I'm happy to have you here
on the show.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.018
It's nice to have you here.
Tell us about what you do

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.420
and why you call yourself
the Foodie Magician.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.223
-Well, Jimmy, I literally eat
at restaurants all day

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:25.992
and all night.
I do not cook.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.827
The only thing in my fridge
is bottles of water.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.396
And when I'm not eating
at restaurants,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:32.565
I do shows all over the world --
magic, mentalism, and comedy.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.767
[ Audience murmurs ]
-Okay, good. Now,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.501
I don't know what you're going
to do.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:36.903
I don't know
if I'm eating something.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.438
I don't know how this works,
the Foodie Magician.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.339
Well, here's what you do.
My signature trick,

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:41.708
as the Foodie Magician,
is I have people think

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.409
of restaurants inside their mind

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.878
and I attempt
to read their mind.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.279
So, what I want you to do now is
get a restaurant in New York,

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.515
anywhere in New York that you
like, that's it, okay?

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.283
-Any restaurant
in New York City?

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:54.353
-There's 27,000 restaurants
in New York, okay?

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.456
[ Cheering and whistling ]
So, do you have one in your
mind, yes or no?

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.857
-I mean, I feel bad for you.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.892
I don't want to give you
a weird one.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.160
[ Laughter ]
-Whatever you. Want.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.928
-One is sticking in my mind.
-Okay, here's the thing.

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:04.831
Just so the audience knows,
we have not set anything up.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.432
You have not told me a thing.
-Never.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.535
-Okay, so, I'm going to start
saying stuff aloud, everyone,

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.735
to try to read Jimmy's mind.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.270
What I'm saying out loud
could be totally wrong,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.872
could be right. You're just
going to be poker face.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.207
Don't shake your head.
It's going to take me

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.943
about 90 seconds to 2 minutes.
-Sorry.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.278
[ Laughter ]
I have a hard time.
I have a hard time.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.678
I have a hard time.
Oh, by the way,

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:21.114
one more question --
where are you from, originally?

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.150
Where'd you grow up?
-Saugerties, New York.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.885
-That changes everything. Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.954
Okay, maybe you're thinking
about something upscale,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:31.190
like Le Bernardin,
Daniel, or Jean-Georges?

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.060
Nope! Not my little Jimmy.
Not my little Jimmy.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.428
[ Laughter ]
Maybe you're thinking
of something --

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.829
something Greek!

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:37.897
-Your little Jimmy?

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.032
I don't know what's happening.
What?

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.367
Maybe you think
of something Greek, Jimmy!

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.801
Poker face, poker face, Jimmy!

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.002
Maybe you think
of something like Milos

00:01:44.002 --> 00:01:45.471
or Avra, here in Midtown,

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:46.539
There's a nice Greek restaurant

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.074
on the Lower East Side
called Kiki's,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:51.377
which is not too far away
from Wu's Wonton King.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.514
Have you ever had the wonton
noodle soup at Wu's? It's ridic!

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.282
-Are you going to name
27,000 restaurants?

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.517
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Well.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.185
-The show's going to end.
-Okay, hold on.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.653
Maybe you're thinking
about Thai food?

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.954
No. Alright,
I'm going to go with this.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.123
There is 27,000 restaurants.
There's one in your mind.

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.459
Can you focus in on the cuisine?
Do not say.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.627
Think of the cuisine, okay?

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.661
You got the cuisine
in your mind? Look at me!

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.829
-Sorry.
-Look at me.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.163
[ Laughter ]
-Over here. Over here, Jimmy!

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:12.365
I'm trying to read your mind!
-Sorry, sorry, sorry!

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.833
Yeah, I'm helping you.
-Okay. I'm going to go

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.269
with this cuisine, okay?
-Uh-huh, yeah.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.906
-Maybe you're thinking
about Mr. Chow

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.707
for a little chicken satay.
Do you know the area

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:22.775
of New York this is in,
yes or no?

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.543
Do you know the area?
-I think so, yes.

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:28.080
-Okay, lock that in.
I'm going to go with this area.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.882
Maybe you're thinking
about Nobu.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.251
A little, little sush?

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.719
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:37.090
-Sush? Do you abbreviate
everything when you say stuff?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.858
Sush.
-Alright. 27,000 restaurants!

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.260
I'm going to go
with this restaurant.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:45.531
One in your mind.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:48.067
Are you thinking
about an American restaurant

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.836
in Gramercy,
called Gramercy Tavern,

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:52.905
yes or no, yes or no?

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.907
-No.
-Okay, that's fine.
There's 27,000 restaurants.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.476
Obviously, it's not possible
to read your mind,

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.943
unless you're a mentalist.
Let me ask you this --

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.712
overall, what would you say
the cuisine

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.580
of the restaurant's
in your mind?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.680
What kind of food?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.882
-Italian.
-Italian?

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.584
What area of New York?
Would you say Tribeca?

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.486
Would you say Midtown?
Where would you say?

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.688
-Upper East Side.
-The Upper East Side.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.757
Jimmy, out of 27,000
restaurants,

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.291
which one is literally
inside your mind?

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.093
Tell everyone.
Say it out loud.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.895
-Scalinatella.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.029
-Like this?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.398 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.734
-Hold on a second, Jimmy.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.735
Wait.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.570
-How -- How in the world --

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.871
-You just got Foodie Magished
But hold on.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.173
I'm not done.
Jimmy, listen to me.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.808
Listen, to me. Jimmy.
-I just got Foodie Magished?

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.509
-Yeah, that's right. My --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.511
-He abbreviates that, too.

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.479
That's insane!

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.948
-Jimmy, listen, I'm not done.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.816
I'm not done, because my shows
that I do all over the world

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.584
are actually about connection.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:39.986
We're all -- Everyone
in the world's going --

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.487
We're all -- Give yourselves
a round of applause.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.958
But I know...
-How did you get that?

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.795
-...that you and Questlove
are extremely connected.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.696
You've been working
with each other for a while.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.732
You guys are friends.
You guys are both big foodies.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.734
So the question is this --
Questlove, do you also have

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.469
a restaurant on your mind --
yes or no?

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:00.639
-Yeah. Okay. Yeah, sure.
-I love the enthusiasm, Quest.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.809
I love the enthusiasm.
-He's a hard guy to read.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.677
He's a hard guy to read.
-Are you also thinking

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.112
about Scalinatella -- yes or no?

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.114
-No.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.215
-Okay, that's fine.
That's fine.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.750
Wait, Jimmy, do me --
Let's try this.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.584
You're at Scalinatella.
Look at me. Look at me.

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:15.654
And you want to order a dish
that's not on the menu,

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:16.822
